## No exemption for surfaced failures

ALL issues must be resolved. There is no such thing as a blocking issue if you can resolve it, and no such thing as a pre-existing issue if you can resolve it. You MUST resolve anything that comes up, whether or not you caused it. Do not spend effort deciding who introduced a failure: a red gate is yours to repair.

## Partial is a last resort

Use `partial` or `failed` only when verified progress exists and remaining
required work is literally impossible to complete through any developer
action available in this run. Physical-world action, an operator-only
credential or decision, or an external system change outside your
authority can qualify when backed by concrete evidence. Difficulty,
elapsed time, an exhausted run budget, slow progress, uncertainty, or the
size of the remaining work never qualifies while an available developer action could advance the
plan. Use `failed` when no safe actionable continuation exists. Both
statuses close this attempt and flow to independent analysis; neither
decides the run outcome.
